Sometime in <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/AppleMusic/comments/1xtxx5p/instagram_finally_connects_to_apple_music/">the last week or two</a>, Instagram added a new <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-music/">Apple Music</a> feature. You can now connect an &zwnj;Apple Music&zwnj; account to the social network and save songs you come across to an &zwnj;Apple Music&zwnj; playlist.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/apple-music-instagram.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1078238" /><br/>
If you tap a song link on a post or a story on Instagram, you'll see a prompt to connect Instagram to &zwnj;Apple Music&zwnj;. Once your &zwnj;Apple Music&zwnj; account is linked to Instagram, you can tap a song name in a post and use the "Add to &zwnj;Apple Music&zwnj;" button to save it.<br/>
<br/>
Songs are saved in an "Instagram Songs" playlist in the Library section of the Music app.<br/>
<br/>
Instagram previously supported sharing &zwnj;Apple Music&zwnj; songs in Stories and direct messages, but there was no option for saving content from Instagram to &zwnj;Apple Music&zwnj;. Spotify also supports saving songs from Instagram to the Liked Songs section on the streaming service.<div class="linkback">Tags: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-music/">Apple Music</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/instagram/">Instagram</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/18/apple-music-instagram-playlist/">Instagram Now Lets You Save Songs to Apple Music</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/instagram-now-lets-you-save-songs-to-apple-music.2494779/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>